{"title": "The Tumbatorium", "pageid": 2093, "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><b><figure class=\"thumb  show-info-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\" style=\"width: 266px\"> \t<a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/princeofyander/images/2/27/The_Tumbatorium.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20100806153929\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"An artists depiction of the Tumbatorium of Tumba.\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/princeofyander/images/2/27/The_Tumbatorium.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/266?cb=20100806153929\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"266\" height=\"274\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-image-name=\"The Tumbatorium.jpg\" data-image-key=\"The_Tumbatorium.jpg\" data-relevant=\"1\" /></a> \t \t<figcaption class=\"thumbcaption\"> \t\t \t\t\t<a href=\"/wiki/File:The_Tumbatorium.jpg\" class=\"info-icon\"><svg><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-info-small\"></use></svg></a> \t\t \t\t \t\t \t\t\t<p class=\"caption\">An artists depiction of the Tumbatorium of Tumba.</p> \t\t \t</figcaption> </figure></b><p><b><i>The Tumbatorium</i> </b>is the embodiment of chaos<i>, </i>also sentient and capable of manifesting as a giant serpent, and of creating semi-solid projections similar to pattern-ghosts. It claims that the <i><a href=\"/wiki/Jewel_of_Judgement\" title=\"Jewel of Judgement\">Jewel of Judgement</a></i> was its eye, stolen by the <i><a href=\"/wiki/The_Unicorn\" title=\"The Unicorn\">Unicorn</a></i>; it appears to desire to return all existence to the primal chaos from which it came.\n</p><h2><span id=\"Location_.26_Appearance\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Location_&amp;_Appearance\">Location &amp; Appearance</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Sign in to edit\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"log-in-edit-section\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fprinceofamber.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FThe_Tumbatorium%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D1&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section\" data-testid=\"log-in-edit-section\" aria-label=\"Sign in to edit\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the Courts of Tumba exists the Tumbatorium, a three dimensional construct that is the opposite number to the <i><a href=\"/wiki/The_Pattern\" title=\"The Pattern\">Pattern</a></i> of <i><a href=\"/wiki/Yander\" title=\"Yander\">Yander</a></i>.<sup> </sup>Where the unchanging, rigid Pattern represents Umba, the Tumbatorium is constantly altering its shape and represents the principle of Tumba. The Tumbatorium appears as a tentacular force that must be navigated on a magical/mental level. Those who navigate this construct successfully gain power over, and the ability to travel through, <i><a href=\"/wiki/Shadow\" title=\"Shadow\">Shadow</a></i>. An additional power gained from the successful navigation of the Tumbatorium is the ability to \"pull\" desired, non-specific objects out of Shadow worlds.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Navigation\">Navigation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Sign in to edit\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"log-in-edit-section\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fprinceofamber.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FThe_Tumbatorium%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D2&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section\" data-testid=\"log-in-edit-section\" aria-label=\"Sign in to edit\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Negotiating the Tumbatorium is extremely difficult and potentially fatal. Prospective initiates of the Tumbatorium generally receive advanced training, but success is dependent less on knowledge than on will. In addition to the danger of dying, some who have attempted the Tumbatorium have experienced permanent cerebral damage, though this fate tends to happen only to those who are weak willed or not of full chaosian blood. Luckily those of chaosian blood usually only end up being insane for a short period of time. Negotiating both the Tumbatorium and the Pattern, as <a href=\"/wiki/Moorlin\" title=\"Moorlin\">Moorlin</a> has, is a uniquely daring feat.\n</p><p>Just as <a href=\"/wiki/Qweryin\" title=\"Qweryin\">Qweryin</a> is keeper of the Pattern, <a href=\"/wiki/Suhuy\" title=\"Suhuy\">Suhuy</a> is the keeper of the Tumbatorium and is a member of the noble houses of Tumba.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Sign in to edit\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"log-in-edit-section\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fprinceofamber.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FThe_Tumbatorium%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D3&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section\" data-testid=\"log-in-edit-section\" aria-label=\"Sign in to edit\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/The_Pattern\" title=\"The Pattern\">The Pattern</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260502163621\nCache expiry: 1209600\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.008 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.013 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 18/1000000\nPost‐